<title>CHINA: China plans to set up housing bank.</title>
<headline>China plans to set up housing bank.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>China plans to set up a state bank to help finance individuals buy apartments, the China Securities Newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said such a bank would provide mortgage loans to private house buyers at interest rates lower than the market level, to help boost the bearish property market.</p>
<p>To encourage private buyers, the payback period could be extended to more than 20 years, it said without giving details.</p>
<p>Currently, only some of China's commercial banks are allowed to provide loans of up to 10 years to home-buyers at market rates.</p>
</text>
